# macOS
.DS_Store
._*

# MATLAB generated / transient
slprj/
codegen/
*.mex*
*.slxc

# Analysis outputs — these are produced per dataset, not part of the toolkit.
# Tool 1 writes tracks/, Tool 2/3 write analysis/ inside the PROJECT folder the user picks,
# so they normally live outside this repo; these entries only matter if a project is opened here.
tracks/
analysis/

# Per-dataset calibration, written by spt_analyze_app's writeCalib into the project folder — or, when
# no tracks/ subfolder resolves, into whatever folder was opened. That is how one ended up committed
# at the repo root, and it kept coming back dirty: MATLAB stamps the write time into every .mat
# header, so re-saving identical values still produces a binary diff.
#
# It also matters that cs_config() with NO argument reads cs_calib.mat from the CURRENT DIRECTORY, so
# a stray one here is silently picked up by any paper script run from the repo root — a second,
# invisible source of a calibration. It is never a source file; it belongs to whichever dataset
# produced it.
cs_calib.mat
